 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It varies a lot depending on you and the weather, a good rule of thumb is drinking a little more than you thirsty until you get a feel for it, then adjust according to the ride. Fill a bottle just before you leave and refill every few hours. You' usually find yourself wanting one after an hour anyway. A light snack half way keeps energy levels up, something sugary sweet if you start to flag. Some people can, but it' usually a good idea to eat something small before a long ride, an empty stomach can make you feel grouchy.",
